decision: changes-requested

Three prior findings are fixed; **R3-N9 and R3-N10 remain partial**. Four blockers remain:

- **N11 — high:** [validate_scope.go:172](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:172). The helper returns the first matching dependency before discovered dependencies are filtered. With modules `a`, `a/nested`, and `b`, `b.dependsOn: ["a", "."]`, and a change inside `a/nested`, the discovered `a` match masks the eligible root dependency. `b` can be carried; reversing dependency order selects it. Evaluate every eligible match.
- **N12 — high:** [validate.go:1431](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1431). A material-changing HEAD transition clears `material_clean` but leaves the original material bindings intact. Delivery parsing ignores `material_clean`; after restoring the earlier source, those bindings can make the incorrectly attributed pass current again. Invalidate unverifiable bindings before publication.
- **N13 — medium:** [validate_carry.go:110](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:110). `EvalSymlinks` does not identify case aliases on case-insensitive Unix filesystems. An override `A` can alias discovered module `a`, pass this guard, and retain results when `a` changes. Check physical directory identity or conservatively refuse alias reuse.
- **N14 — high:** [validate.go:1167](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1167). HEAD is captured after carry selection. If selection finishes at H0 and HEAD advances to H1 before capture, old results can receive H1 provenance while the final head comparison passes. Capture and pin the subject before planning.

These are code-inspection findings. Additional reproduction fixtures, including a case-insensitive filesystem probe, were unavailable because scratch storage is read-only.

Focused and broader tests, race tests, vet, and strict artifact-check passed. Both required matrix runs failed on sandbox write restrictions. The sealed canonical record has 236 passes; fresh required-tool validation remains unmet.

Applied the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.

